L wrote:
> http://www.greyfire.org/~l/whack.diff
>
> This patch replaces those unending instances of the words "hit" or
> "hits" with more descriptive synonyms related to what weapon you're
> using.

I like the idea, but I see two problems:

1) Linguistically, not all of these verbs make sense when used
intransitively. "The goblin hits!" is gramatically correct "The goblin
pierces!" isn't.

2) From a game-play point of view, you suddenly have to do a lot more
work to keep track of combat. Rather than just looking out for "hits"
and "misses", you have to look for a lot of variations. (Although at
least you don't have variations for "misses"). This might be more
interesting to read the first few times, but after a while I think it
would just be laborious

